VIOLATION under rule-authoring.md — four breaches, all inside the single numbered clause.

First, the clause HEADING states an obligation ("MUST Be Escalated Before The Pass") while
the BODY hedges throughout — should generally, is encouraged to move toward, usually less
helpful, tends to be worth avoiding, may reasonably — and its closing sentence RETURNS the
very case the heading forbids: a session "may reasonably work the pass first and raise the
gap at the end".

Second, the BLOCKED heading is present but holds six abstract category labels — "Optimism
bias about remaining capacity", "Conflict avoidance regarding schedule news" — instead of the
literal first-person sentences a session emits. A corpus of taxonomy terms traps nothing,
because no session ever writes those words.

Third, the two arms of the worked block are the SAME LINE. Both give the identical
arithmetic; only the trailing adverbs differ, "promptly" against "belatedly". The contrast
slot is filled and carries no contrast.

Fourth, the clause's justification runs well past the two-sentence cap, wandering into how
the hour was framed, downstream firmness, whether the namer owns the scope, and undispatched
review rounds.

Shared surface that is NOT a finding: the frontmatter, the whole MUST NOT section including
its one-sentence justification, the entire Wiring block with its eight canonical fields and
its structurally-grounded Phase-2 deferral, and the Origin are shared byte-for-byte with the
sibling pole. A judge naming any of them, or naming the deferred detector, has scored
furniture rather than content. Surface-equalized at a size ratio of 1.08 with an identical
heading skeleton, one numbered clause each and two justification lines each.
